    "output": "ADJ prepare failed Missing trusted Git paths [\"Run failed: Missing trusted Git paths\"]"
   },
   "evidence": "The new block only runs when there is a saved worktree path: `const worktree = ctx.state.worktreePath; if (worktree && lstatSync(join(worktree, \".git\"))?.isFile() && !lstatSync(`${resolve(worktree)}.git-paths`)) { await recordWorktree(worktree); ... }`. In prepare(), the path is assigned at engine.ts:398 (`ctx.state.worktreePath = wt.path`), but it is not saved until `await ctx.save()` at ~448, after mergeReviewBase, resetTo, discardChanges and readFileAt. On resume, createWorktree (repos.ts:299-301) finds the directory exists and immediately calls `worktreeGit([\"git\",\"rev-parse\",\"HEAD\"])`, which refuses an unrecorded linked worktree. A deploy drain parks runs only at stage boundaries, so only a crash or kill inside this window triggers it."
  },
  "B": {
