    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/legacy-adjudication.ts\"",
    "output": "{\"claim\":\"C1\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"error\":\"Missing trusted Git paths\",\"recordExists\":false,\"legacyLogCount\":0,\"failures\":[\"Run failed: Missing trusted Git paths\"]}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary script created a genuine linked worktree using plain git worktree add, without a sidecar, and called executeRun with persisted preparation state lacking worktreePath. HEAD gates registration on `const worktree = ctx.state.worktreePath; if (worktree && ...)`. Preparation subsequently calls createWorktree at engine.ts:389; its existing-directory branch calls `worktreeGit([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], { cwd: path })` at repos.ts:301 before recording anything. The path is assigned at engine.ts:398 and saved later at :449. Base has the same preparation/reuse ordering but no legacy-registration block, so this is an explicitly requested recovery case left unfixed."
  }
